{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-brings-smoothness-chart-regularity","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:brings-smoothness-chart-regularity","kind":"remark","title":"Regularity of the Briggs--Klein chart","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-brings-smoothness-resolution","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-briggs-klein-chart"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-brings-smoothness-resolution","tags":["brings-surface","smooth","resolution","branch-point","color"],"text":"brings-smoothness-chart-regularity.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:brings-smoothness-chart-regularity\"></a><p>Beyond <a href=\"#prop:brings-smoothness-resolution\">smoothness and intrinsic resolution</a>, the Briggs--Klein chart is regular: the radial parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r = \\lvert w_1 \\rvert^2</code> is a regular function on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}</code>, and the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">C_5</code> orbits <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">w_k \\mapsto \\zeta^k w_k</code> foliate <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}</code> without fixed points for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0 &#x3C; r &#x3C; \\infty</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-smoothness-chart-regularity.md","heading":"Remark","number":"7.7.3"}
